  <text xml:lang="grc"><body xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.dindorf1893-grc1"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.dindorf1893-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros"><head>ΑΛΕΞΑΝΔΡΟΣ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-1" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:43">
            <note type="source">1. Stobaeus Floril. CXXIV, 20.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Παλαιὰ καινοῖς δακρύοις οὐ χρὴ στένειν.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Priami verba esse videntur. Cf. fgm. II.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-2" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:44">
            <note type="source">2. Stobaeus CXIV, 7.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Α. Οἶδ᾽· ἀλλὰ κάμπτειν τῷ χρόνῳ λύπας χρεών.</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">Β. Χρή· τοῦτο δ᾽ εἰπεῖν ῥᾷον ἢ φέρειν κακά.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="3" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-3" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:45">
            <note type="source">3. Stobaeus CV, 38.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ὥστ᾽ οὔτις ἀνδρῶν εἰς ἅπαντ᾽ εὐδαιμονεῖ.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Priami (cf. fgm. II.) aut chori Hecubam consolantis sunt verba. Ad sententiam cf. Stheneb. fgm. I.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="4" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-4" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:46">
            <note type="source">4. Stobaeus CVIII, 17.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Πάντων τὸ θανεῖν· τὸ δὲ κοινὸν ἄχος</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">μετρίως ἀλγεῖν σοφία μελετᾷ.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Chori esse eodem modo Hecubam consolantis perspicuum est.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="5" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-5" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:47">
            <note type="source">5. Stobaeus IV, 32.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ὅθεν δὲ νικᾶν χρῆν σε, δυστυχεῖς, ἄναξ,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ὅθεν δέ σ᾽ οὐ χρῆν, εὐτυχεῖς· δούλοισι γὰρ</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">τοῖς σοῖσι νικᾷς, τοῖς δ᾽ ἐλευθέροισιν οὔ.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="6" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-6" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:48">
            <note type="source">6. Stobaeus LXII, 14.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Σοφὸς μὲν οὖν εἶ, Πρίαμ᾽, ὅμως δέ σοι λέγω</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">δούλου φρονοῦντος μᾶλλον ἢ φρονεῖν χρεὼν</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">οὐκ ἔστιν ἄχθος μεῖζον, οὐδὲ δώμασι</l>
              <l n="4" xml:lang="grc">κτῆσις κακίων οὐδ᾽ ἀνωφελεστέρα.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. V.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="7" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-7" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:51">
            <note type="source">7. Stobaeus LXII, 19.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">δούλους γὰρ οὐ</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">καλὸν πεπᾶσθαι κρείσσονας τῶν δεσποτῶν.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. V.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="8" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-8" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:50">
            <note type="source">8. Stobaeus LXII, 16.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Δούλων ὅσοι φιλοῦσι δεσποτῶν γένος,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">πρὸς τῶν ὁμοίων πόλεμον αἱροῦνται μέγαν.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. V.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="9" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-9" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:59">
            <note type="source">9. Stobaeus LXIX, 20.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἐκ τῶν ὁμοίων οἱ κακοὶ γαμοῦσ᾽ ἀεί.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. V.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="10" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-10" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:49">
            <note type="source">10. Stobaeus LXII, 15.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἤλεγχον· οὕτω γὰρ κακὸν δοῦλον γένος·</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">γαστὴρ ἅπαντα, τὠπίσω οὐδὲν σκοπεῖ.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. V.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="11" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-11" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:53">
            <note type="source">11. Stobaeus LXXXVI, 7.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Οὐκ ἔστιν ἐν κακοῖσιν εὐγένεια,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">παρ᾽ ἀγαθοῖσι δ᾽ ἀνδρῶν.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="12" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-12" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:56">
            <note type="source">12. Stobaeus XLII, 3.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἄναξ, διαβολαὶ δεινὸν ἀνθρώποις κακόν</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ἀγλωσσίᾳ δὲ πολλάκις ληφθεὶς ἀνὴρ</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">δίκαια λέξας ἧσσον εὐγλώσσου φέρει.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="13" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-13" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:61">
            <note type="source">13. Orion Anthologn. I, 3. p. 41 ed. Schneidew.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Μισῶ</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">σοφὸν ἐν λόγοισιν, ἐς δ᾽ ὄνησιν οὐ σοφόν.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. XII.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="14" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-14" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:55">
            <note type="source">14. Stobaeus XCIII, 14.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἄδικον δ᾽ ὁ πλοῦτος, πολλὰ δ᾽ οὐκ ὀρθῶς ποιεῖ.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. XII.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="15" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-15" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:54">
            <note type="source">15. Stobaeus XCVII, 3.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Κακόν τι παίδευμ᾽ ἦν ἄρ᾽ εἰς εὐανδρίαν</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ὁ πλοῦτος ἀνθρώποισιν αἵ τ᾽ ἄγαν τρυφαί.</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">πενία δὲ δύστηνον μὲν, ἀλλ᾽ ὅμως τρέφει</l>
              <l n="4" xml:lang="grc">μοχθοῦντ᾽ ἀμείνω τέκνα καὶ δραστήρια.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. XII.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="16" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-16" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:57">
            <note type="source">16. Stobaeus LXII, 18.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ὦ παγκάκιστοι καὶ τὸ δοῦλον οὐ λόγῳ</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ἔχοντες, ἀλλὰ τῇ τύχῃ κεκτημένοι.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Cf. fgm. XII.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="17" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-17" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros">
            <note type="source">17. Stobaeus LXXXVI, 2.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Περισσόμυθος ὁ λόγος, εὐγένειαν εἰ</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">βρότειον εὐλογήσομεν· τὸ γὰρ πάλαι</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">πρῶτον ὅτ᾽ ἐγενόμεθα</l>
              <l n="4" xml:lang="grc">διὰ δ᾽ ἔκρινεν ἁ</l>
              <l n="5" xml:lang="grc">τεκοῦσα γὰ βροτοὺς, ὁμοί-</l>
              <l n="6" xml:lang="grc">αν χθὼν ἅπασιν ἐξεπαίδευσεν ὅ-</l>
              <l n="7" xml:lang="grc">ψιν</l>
              <l n="8" xml:lang="grc">Ἴδιον οὐδὲν ἔχομεν·</l>
              <l n="9" xml:lang="grc">τία δὲ γονὰ τὸ τ᾽ εὐγενὲς καὶ τὸ δυσ-</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="18" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-18" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:58">
            <note type="source">18. Stobaeus XXXVIII, 20.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Οἴ μοι, θανοῦμαι διὰ τὸ χρήσιμον φρενῶν,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ὁ τοῖσιν ἄλλοις γίγνεται σωτηρία.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="19" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-19" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:62">
            <note type="source">19. Stobaeus CXI, 8.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἑκάβη, τὸ θεῖον ὡς ἄελπτον ἔρχεται</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">θνητοίσιν, ἕλκει δ᾽ οὔποτ᾽ ἐκ ταὐτοῦ τύχας.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="20" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-20" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros">
            <note type="source">20. Plut. rei publ. gerend. præc. 28, p. 821 Β.</note>
            <quote>Ὥσπερ οὖν τῆς Κασάνδρας ἀδοξούσης ἀνόνητος ἦν ἡ μαντικὴ τοῖς πολίταις·</quote>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἄκραντα γάρ μ᾽ ἔθηκε θεσπίζειν θεὸς,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">καὶ πρὸς παθόντων καν κακοῖσι κειμένων</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">σοφὴ κέκλημαι, πρὶν παθεῖν δὲ μαίνομαι.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="21" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-21" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:60">
            <note type="source">21. Clem. Alexandr. Strom. VI, 2, 10. (p. 742 P.)</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Χρόνος δὲ δείξει σ᾽ ᾧ τεκμηρίῳ μαθὼν</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ἢ χρηστὸν ὄντα γνώσομαι σε γ᾽ ἢ κακόν.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="22" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-22" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros">
            <note type="source">22. Longin. de Sublim. c. 15.</note>
            <quote>Ὅμοια καὶ Εὐριπίδης τὰ ἐπὶ τῆς Κασάνδρας αὐτῷ (Εὐριπίδῃ)·</quote>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἀλλ᾽ ὦ φίλιπποι Τρῶες—</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="23" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-23" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:42">
            <note type="source">23. Schol. Aristoph. Ran. 100. ad Aristophanis verba: αἰθέρα Διὸς δωμάτιον ἢ χρόνου πόδα adnotat: —τὸ δὲ χρόνου πόδα ἐστὶν ἐξ Ἀλεξάνδρας (ἀλεξάνδρου. Rav. Ven.).</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">καὶ χρόνου προὔβαινε πούς.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="24" xml:id="fragment-alexandros-dindorf1893_grc1-24" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_alexandros" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.alexandros.nauck1889grc1:63">
            <note type="source">24. Hesych. Ἄρρητος κόρη· ἡ Περσεφόνη. Εὐριπίδης Ἀλεξάνδρα. Eodem modo loquutus est in Helen. 1307. cf. Carcin. ap. Diod. Sic. V. 5. λέγουσι Δήμητρός ποτ᾽ ἄρρητον κόρην Πλούτωνα κρυφίοις ἁρπάσαι βουλεύμασιν.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Ex Euripidis Alexandro porro petitum censet Gaisfordius versum, quem Stobæus LXVII, 12. c. lemmate Ἀλεξάνδρου affert:</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">ταμεῖον ἀρετῆς ἐστι γενναία γυνή.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Quem ab Euripide profectum esse non credam, quum et aliena sit ab Atticorum usu ταμεῖον forma, quam omnes codd. præbent, et, si ea in ταμιεῖον mutaretur, quod facili negotio a Meinekio Poet. com. I, p. 488 factum est, Euripidem tam frigida ac tragœdiæ parum convenienter dicere ἀρετῆς ταμιεῖον potuisse, mihi nemo persuadeat. In comœdia reperitur Phœnicidis ταμιεῖον ap. Ath. X, p. 415 E; significat autem cellam penuariam. Quare aut cum Naekio (sched. crit. p. 7.) versum Alexandro Ætolo, aut rectius, ut mihi videtur, Alexandro, comico poetæ (de quo vide Meinek. 1. c. p. 487.) tribueris.</note>
          </div>
        </div></body></text></TEI>
